    "winner": "kime",
    "clashSummary": "K.I.M.E vs SEVZ took place at **PenGame Rap Battle 2025**, during the **Cold War Finals event** at **Ministry of Sound**. The battle is hosted after the main Cold War tournament action, with judges **Harry Pinero**, **Professor Green**, and **Abra Kadabra** present.\n\nSEVZ wins the coin toss and chooses K.I.M.E to go first.\n\nK.I.M.E opens with a strong round built around confidence, physical threat and school/classroom imagery. He starts by saying there are many Black youths trying to rap, but outside battle they would get wrapped too. He tells SEVZ to take the L back to his classroom, says he will happy slap him, backhand him, make him cartwheel, and uses smoke, caliber, candy crush, bluff, college and family material. The round is packed and aggressive, with K.I.M.E presenting himself as the more dangerous and direct battler.\n\nSEVZ responds with a sharper performance round. He opens by saying it is time to go again and that if K.I.M.E is not dead already, he will “dupie” him now. He attacks K.I.M.E through Joker/Pennywise imagery, his girlfriend, money, height, age, auntie/mum material, Ra’Siah’s counter reference, fake friends, PenGame status and veteran experience. His round has more character and more performance control, but K.I.M.E’s first is still strong enough to keep it close.\n\nRound two is where both battlers raise the level. K.I.M.E uses a dense run of personal insults, including “Bar Bar Blackley,” backstreet/backseat wordplay, Purple Aki family material, gangrene, father/parentage jokes, sister material, virginity, Chlamydia, Top Boy, rock bottom, “Balamin,” Madeleine McCann reference, battery, Halloween, Vaseline, Barking/Battersea and galaxy imagery. It is his most technical and layered round.\n\nSEVZ’s second is arguably his best round. He opens with politics/North Korea/Kim Jong Un wordplay, saying K.I.M.E came from the north to kill his own career. He then calls him a black hobbit, black leprechaun, sends him over the rainbow, uses jackpot/adblock, Martin Luther King/Santa’s little helpers, Orion replacement, black dwarf, beard/pigeon, lisp/saliva, Sun Jin-Woo, blueprint, broken home, back-to-back, shoulder-to-shoulder, older/colder, and thick/flat “dum dum” material. The round gets big reaction and feels like SEVZ’s clearest round win.\n\nRound three becomes the deciding round. K.I.M.E brings a grime-flavoured final round, shouting out Manchester and PenGame North. He tells SEVZ to respect his elder, brings belt/shelter/lightning/Delta imagery, attacks SEVZ’s girlfriend, hygiene, lies, lack of heart, feet/defeat wordplay, South Park-style switching, Kucha/dildo material, girlfriend/body jokes, choir/gospel image, nostril/Efton comparison, dad/fatherhood angle and ends by saying SEVZ just got slain by K.I.M.E. The round has strong presence and sounds like a proper final push.\n\nSEVZ’s third is also strong. He attacks K.I.M.E’s bald head, accent, breath, Kanye West compressed, plastic/Kim Kardashian, lane/status, DDG/empty, grave/empty bladder, flowers/shower, tower, Gucci/GG, and keeps pressure with his usual confidence. It is clean and polished, but the judges lean toward K.I.M.E overall.\n\nThe official decision goes to **K.I.M.E**.\n\nHarry Pinero says both were lyrical, but he preferred K.I.M.E because of delivery and the sense of story. Professor Green says it is difficult and acknowledges both rounds, but also chooses K.I.M.E. Abra Kadabra says K.I.M.E did just enough and calls for a rematch.\n\nThe decision is controversial in the room, with some crowd disagreement, but the official result is **K.I.M.E wins**.",
