    "tag": "Christmas Special",
    "clashSummary": "TRAPPY vs iiiBEREALZ, also referred to throughout the transcript as **I.B. Rules**, took place at the **PenGame Rap Battle Christmas Special** in the dungeon. The host introduces it as a highly anticipated battle and makes it clear that this one had to go down without judges interfering.\n\nTRAPPY wins the coin toss and goes first.\n\nTRAPPY opens with a strong first round built around food, cake and battle status. He starts with eggshells, sugar, flour and cake imagery, flipping iiiBEREALZ’s cake business into a setup. He says iiiBEREALZ was meant to advance, but someone else stood in his place, then ties egg, sugar and flour together as ingredients. He follows with One Punch Man / manga imagery, says iiiBEREALZ cried after FENDRY, mocks his body, sweating, cakes and supply, then compares both of their tournament losses. He says iiiBEREALZ got robbed against FENDRY, while people said TRAPPY got robbed too. The round also has side-quest/final-boss material, Saturn/halo/head imagery, Drake/singing material and body/weight insults.\n\niiiBEREALZ replies with a strong first of his own. He says he will not hold back and that his bars hold weight, then attacks TRAPPY’s videos, image, cake angle, teeth, name, battle history and alleged bar stealing. He says TRAPPY tried to kill him three times and got bodied each time, then accuses him of stealing bars from other battlers and recycling old material. The round is direct and gives iiiBEREALZ a strong counter-frame: TRAPPY is not original, not authentic and not as dangerous as he thinks.\n\nRound two is TRAPPY’s best round. He attacks iiiBEREALZ’s “top five on PenGame” claim, says he is only target practice, then breaks down iiiBEREALZ’s battle record. He names JC, RA’SIAH, CHEEKZ, KARMA, FENDRY, DANIEL and others, arguing that iiiBEREALZ has no title, no accolades, no finals and no real payback moments. He also attacks the “I.B. Rules” name, says his talent is wasted, accuses him of copying from DAN and ORION, and gives him a “C minus grade” as if he belongs back in PenGame Academy.\n\niiiBEREALZ’s second is aggressive and personal. He says he has poured blood, sweat and tears into PenGame, then attacks TRAPPY as cross-eyed, cliché, musically weak, badly engineered, gap-toothed, blind to facts and full of ego. He also brings up TRAPPY fainting at the finals, says he stole from Tay Roc and Chess, and calls him a thief. The round is strong, but TRAPPY’s second is more structured and more opponent-specific.\n\nRound three decides the battle. TRAPPY opens by asking if iiiBEREALZ is complacent or allergic to levelling up. He attacks him as underdeveloped despite being a veteran, says having three “I”s in the name still does not mean he can see, criticises him for going overtime, says his blood will be left on the wall like Banksy, and brings up women, league politics, outside-battle respect, internet behaviour and fish-and-ackee imagery. He also addresses his own finals collapse, saying he passed out at PenGame finals because of health and overwork, then flips that back on iiiBEREALZ by saying he is still doing the same thing.\n\niiiBEREALZ closes with the cleanest final round of the battle. He calls himself Hannibal Lecter, says he knows how to dispose of bodies, and repeats that he has been catching bodies on PenGame. He attacks TRAPPY’s looks, name, sight, talent and status, says he is not one of the best but the best indeed, then brings Dejan/napalm, K-Dog, God’s Plan, Mob Ties, Popeye, pencil-full-of-lead, Benson, Batman/Bane, Cain and Abel, Nas / It Was Written, and “I.B. Rules if he asked who did it” wordplay. The host reacts strongly and calls it absolutely cold.\n\nThere is no official decision. The host asks viewers to comment who they think won.\n\nBased on the battle, iiiBEREALZ edges it by Archive Judgement.",
