    "clashSummary": "DRIZZGB vs SEVZ took place at a special **PenGame Rap Battle 2025** event streamed through **Lounges.tv**. The host confirms this is a **one-rounder**, with both battlers getting one extended round to settle it.\n\nDRIZZGB goes first.\n\nDRIZZGB opens by saying it has been a while and he needs to win this one. He attacks SEVZ as young, protected, dependent on his mum, unable to buy Rizla or Red Bull without parental help, and not ready to go bar-for-bar with him. His early angle is simple and effective: SEVZ is too young, too sheltered and not built for the clash.\n\nDRIZZGB then moves into family and body insults, saying SEVZ’s mum still wipes his snot, and using a crude football-pitch image around her body. He builds momentum with lines about “taking liberties,” being better than SEVZ, SEVZ not being built for the clash, and sending him home in an urn. The round has several restarts and interruptions, but he keeps rebuilding it and eventually gets into a strong rhythm.\n\nThe second half of DRIZZGB’s round becomes more aggressive. He talks about blowing smoke in SEVZ’s face, stepping on his face, spitting on his grave, telling him he should be at uni finishing grades rather than battling, then flips SEVZ’s name into “severed up” and “peppered up.” He finishes with violent imagery, Putin war references, Top Boy lines, looting, shooting and ending the clash.\n\nSEVZ responds with a more polished and layered round. He opens by saying DRIZZGB is nowhere near his level, using Rishi Sunak wordplay to say he will send him to the sky. He attacks DRIZZGB as dead already, says DRIZZ should have stayed in a graveyard, then builds into science/chemistry, cousin, Orion ID, false win, N-word pass, cross-eyed jokes, tic-tac-toe, guide dog and smoke-detector imagery.\n\nSEVZ then hits the strongest middle section of the battle. He attacks DRIZZGB’s identity, saying he looks Asian but claims Black and white, compares him to a skunk, says he stinks, calls him a self-proclaimed Lord of the Mics who never got a call-up from Jammer, flips Boy Better Know, JME flow, Rocky and Ivan Drago references, then says DRIZZ wants to be Black but lacks melanin and lives in Trappy’s shadow.\n\nThe round keeps building. SEVZ uses future/vision and blind-man imagery, then goes into an Aladdin/genie scheme, Will Smith/Jada Pinkett Smith crack imagery, criticises DRIZZ for explaining bars live on stage, uses football/referee wordplay, attacks his calibre, says DRIZZ is not a rival or challenger, and ends with adoption/Beverly/Trappy carrying him for nine rounds. The room reacts strongly, and SEVZ’s round feels more complete.\n\nThe host ends by calling it a dope battle and tells viewers to comment who they think won. There is no official judgement.\n\nBased on the performance, structure and reaction, the Archive Judgement goes to **SEVZ**.",
