    "clashSummary": "F-DON vs K.I.M.E, referred to in the transcript as **Efton vs Keem**, took place at a special **PenGame Rap Battle 2025** event streamed through **Lounges.tv**. The host introduces it as a serious clash and calls for crowd interaction, with reloads encouraged if the room hears something they like.\n\nK.I.M.E goes first.\n\nK.I.M.E opens with a long, aggressive round aimed at F-DON’s appearance, age, relationship, music, PenGame history and status. He starts with a heavy nose/nostril angle, saying F-DON’s nostrils are bigger than rockets and that when he breathes, the room rotates. He then moves into a strong Marvel-themed section, referencing Thor, Fantastic Four, Iron Man, Far From Home, No Way Home, Captain America, Black Widow, Infinity War, Endgame, Eternals, Avengers, Venom and Doomsday.\n\nThe Marvel section is one of K.I.M.E’s strongest moments. He uses it to say F-DON is not a hero, not a captain and not someone who will be avenged after losing. From there, K.I.M.E attacks F-DON’s PenGame and Don’t Flop history, says he rents cars for videos but catches buses in real life, attacks his girlfriend, says Dan carried him in the final, and questions his image, sexuality and status.\n\nK.I.M.E finishes with a long “F is for…” breakdown: F is for fake, fabricate, fuckboy and follower. He also attacks F-DON as old, still watching anime, out of touch, short of leadership, and says he will bring him down to size. It is a packed opening round with a lot of material.\n\nF-DON responds with a calmer but more controlled round. He starts by acknowledging that K.I.M.E has some fire, but says K.I.M.E is only a Charmander while he is fully evolved Charizard. He then flips K.I.M.E’s name, age, size, money, lack of crime, lack of bread, card decline, height and lack of punches. His structure is clear: K.I.M.E is younger, smaller, less experienced, poorer and not ready to stand with him.\n\nThe biggest theme of F-DON’s response is shortness. He repeatedly attacks K.I.M.E’s height, saying he should be battling SEVZ, but still makes K.I.M.E look like a boy. He uses “short” in multiple ways: short temper, short bread, short opponent, short money and short ability. It becomes the central thread of his round.\n\nF-DON also builds a bar-fight/bartender scheme, says he treats PenGame like sport but does not like being judged because it reminds him of court, then moves into more direct violence and fire imagery. He talks about breaking K.I.M.E down to components, sending condolences, pulling up with soldiers, being fire and ferocious, returning rewired, and not caring about K.I.M.E bringing up choking or stumbling.\n\nThe host ends the battle without an official judgement and tells viewers to comment who they think won. Based on completion, control and closing strength, this is a close one-rounder, but the Archive Judgement edges to **F-DON**.",
