        "performer": "F-DON",
        "overview": "F-DON wins by Archive Judgement because his response is cleaner, more structured and easier to follow. K.I.M.E has more angles and a stronger technical opening, but F-DON controls the back half of the battle and finishes with more authority.\n\nHis round works because he simplifies the clash. Rather than trying to match K.I.M.E angle-for-angle, he makes the battle about hierarchy: K.I.M.E is smaller, younger, poorer, less experienced and not ready. The Charmander/Charizard opener sets that tone immediately.\n\nThe shortness angle is repetitive but effective. F-DON uses it as a backbone for the round, moving from height jokes into money, sport, women, bread, temper and battle status. Because this is a one-rounder, that repeated theme helps the crowd follow him.\n\nHis best moment is the “bar fight / bartender / shots” section, because it links battle bars with drinking/bar imagery. The “judged / court” line also lands well because it gives the round a real-life edge.\n\nF-DON’s biggest strength is round control. He sounds like someone who knows how to build a response and close it properly.",
