    "clashSummary": "ZEN vs F-DON took place at **PenGame Rap Battle 2025** as the last battle of the night before Cheekz’s performance. The host introduces it as a serious clash and frames it as a battle people had been looking forward to. F-DON calls heads, loses the toss, and ZEN chooses to go first.\n\nZEN opens with a long appearance-based first round. His main target is F-DON’s eyes, nose, face and body shape. He says F-DON’s eyes are so far apart that he needs to check one eye at his own yard and the other at his neighbour’s. He compares F-DON to a hammerhead shark, uses Mo Farah to exaggerate the distance between his eyes, then attacks his long neck, nose, lips, age and frog-like look. The round is packed with visual insults and punchline-heavy writing.\n\nF-DON responds with a strong first round of his own. He opens with a “best player / bed layer / lead sprayer / Zendaya” rhyme pattern and moves into Tory Lanez, Ned Stark, Top Boy, Santan Dave, Skillibeng and “bad man” material. His “she love a bad man” section gets a big reaction, but the round is interrupted when a drink is spilled. F-DON recovers well and continues with house/yard, gratitude, PenGame letting ZEN in, Callaloo, kangaroo pouch and Magaluf material. This round is competitive and probably F-DON’s best.\n\nRound two is where ZEN starts to pull away. He continues with nose and appearance angles, saying F-DON could sniff coke through a garden hose and has a nose like Chris Eubank Senior. He adds chin, rental-car, motorbike, choke, fire, Burner Boy, Denzel, bonfire and Quagmire material. The round is more controlled than F-DON’s second and keeps the pressure on.\n\nF-DON’s second starts well with Leeds, “Kappistan / Kappanese,” capping, martial arts, capoeira, Capricorn and Capri Styles material. However, the round falls apart. He stumbles, and the room reacts strongly. The host makes an executive decision and moves the battle on. This is the decisive turning point.\n\nZEN’s third round is the strongest and clearest round of the battle. He calls it a redemption arc, brings back his “Grandmaster Mic Man” identity, references being a Don’t Flop champ, then attacks F-DON for being on steroids, looking like Deontay Wilder, living in Dan Dannah’s shadow, and not reaching Dan’s level. He uses a Karate Kid/Miyagi/Daniel-son scheme, black belt imagery, his tournament loss, then a long Efton name-flip section. He closes with monster truck, Donald Trump, monk/skunk, T-shirt, Fendi/Fila, Poseidon, Easter Island, home-under-the-hammer and war imagery. It is a proper closing round.\n\nF-DON’s third is shorter and less controlled. He attacks ZEN as being from Leeds, not on anything, capping, “Kappistan / Kappanese,” acapella beating, capoeira, Capricorn, Capri Styles and being an idiot. He also criticises ZEN’s fast delivery, saying half the time he spits too fast and people cannot understand him. The round has some moments, but it does not match ZEN’s third. At the end, F-DON asks to do his first round again, but the host refuses.\n\nThere is no official judgement. The host tells viewers to comment who they think won.\n\nBased on the battle, ZEN wins by Archive Judgement.",
