        "overview": "ZEN wins this battle because he is more complete across the full three rounds. His first is strong, his second clearly beats F-DON’s interrupted second, and his third is the best round of the battle.\n\nZEN’s first round is built almost entirely around physical comedy. He attacks F-DON’s eyes, nose, neck, lips, face and frog-like appearance. The eye-distance angle is the main thread, and he keeps finding new ways to return to it: Specsavers, neighbours, hammerhead shark, Mo Farah and opticians. It is simple but effective.\n\nHis second round continues with appearance but adds more variety. The nose/garden hose, Eubank Senior, chin, rental car, motorbike and fire-name material all give the round more shape. It is not as memorable as the third, but it is controlled.\n\nHis third is the battle-winning round. ZEN speaks on his own status, his tournament loss, his Don’t Flop background and his return. Then he turns F-DON’s relationship with Dan Dannah into the central attack, saying F-DON lives in Dan’s shadow and cannot reach his level. The Karate Kid/Miyagi/Daniel-son section makes the round feel more personal and more layered than his earlier appearance jokes.\n\nZEN’s biggest strength is volume and control. He gives three full rounds and finishes strongest.",
